    {
        "url": "https://x.com/jwt0625/status/2119119436385018045",
        "tweets": [
            {
                "text": "this bare wafer sitting on optical breadboard \"wafer level test setup\" really shows how different industry or even same industry different era folks do things very differently.\nhere is another one: before LN became TFLN, bulk LN folks would scribe the chip/wafer name using a diamond scriber on the backside (now people do proper litho for labels and names), and when they inspect poling domains with HF etch (etch speed is different along crystal +z and -z), they put the wafer on a piece of paper, pour HF, and let its surface tension hold itself within the wafer.. maybe not everyone at the time was doing this cowboy style acid etch.",
                "media": [
                    {
                        "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HWgahDoaAAIvDi3?format=jpg",
                        "local_path": "media/20261107_074606_0.jpg"
                    }
                ],
                "timestamp": "2026-11-07T07:46:06+00:00"
            }
        ]
    },
